CPU backend: the other workstreams' kernel tests on the CPU (patch -p1 from the repo root, against the
native clone's tests/kernels/{test_gemm_w,test_moe_grouped,wformats}.py and the offload clone's
test_cpu_experts.py as of 2026-10-24).

With tests/kernels/conftest.py's LX_BACKEND=cpu (committed in the CPU clone), these tests run against
libdromos_cpu.so. Three things in them are CUDA-specific and are gated on BACKEND == "cuda" here:
the sm_89/sm_80 arch-override families (the CPU's lx_arch is an ISA level, not an SM), the tile-variant
tuner tests (the CPU registers no variants), and the grouped kernel's NOT_SUPPORTED cases for tile shapes
the CUDA kernels cannot take (the CPU takes them). The ctypes lx_weight in wformats.py and
test_cpu_experts.py also gains expert_global, the field Formats added to kernels.h, without which a
backend that reads it gets garbage for NVFP4 stacks.

